[
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a preparation method of a La-Fe-Si-based composite material with good plastic deformation performance, which comprises the following steps: uniformly mixing La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material powder and micron-sized Fe-Ni alloy material powder, and carrying out high-temperature discharge plasma sintering molding to prepare a magnetic refrigeration block material; the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material is a La < 1.0 > Cex (Fe < 1-y > Coy) < 13-z > Siz compound, wherein x is greater than or equal to 0.1 and less than or equal to 0.3, y is greater than or equal to 0.01 and less than or equal to 0.08, z is greater than or equal to 1.0 and less than or equal to 1.6, and the particle size is less than or equal to 90 microns. The preparation method effectively solves the problems that the La-Fe-Si material is poor in processing formability and difficult to consider the magnetocaloric-mechanical synergistic performance. And meanwhile, the process integration level is greatly improved.",
    "applicants": [
      "SOUTH CHINA UNIV OF TECHNOLOGY",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN122013019.A",
    "publicationDate": "20260512",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based composite material with good plastic deformation performance and preparation method of La-Fe-Si-based composite material"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a La-Fe-Si-based layered composite material and a preparation method thereof.The preparation method comprises the following steps that mixed powder is prepared according to a set chemical proportion, and the mixed powder contains La, Fe and Si elements; the mixed powder and Fe or Fe alloy powder are alternately laid, the layered powder is placed in a metal sheath, the metal sheath is pressed and formed in a high-vacuum environment or an inert atmosphere, then annealing treatment is conducted, and the composite material of the layered structure is obtained; and carrying out hydrogen absorption treatment on the layered structure composite material to obtain the La-Fe-Si-based layered composite material. According to the preparation method, La-Fe-Si-based mixed powder and Fe or Fe alloy powder are alternately laid, then the composite material is subjected to large-size uniform deformation through a metal sheath compression molding technology and annealing and hydrogen absorption treatment, an alternate layered structure with a magnetocaloric layer and a non-magnetocaloric layer is achieved, the internal compactness of the layered structure is improved, and the magnetic field performance of the composite material is improved. Pores become fine and dispersed, so that the material has excellent mechanical property, anisotropic heat-conducting property and large magnetocaloric effect.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SHANGHAI",
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "上海大学",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所"
    ],
    "docId": "CN120839070.A",
    "publicationDate": "20251028",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based layered composite material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material based on an FHP technology and a preparation method thereof.The preparation method comprises the following steps that a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material with the particle size smaller than or equal to 100 microns is used as main phase particles, 0-5 wt% of pure Fe powder is added to serve as an adhesive, and pre-compaction is conducted after sufficient mixing; the particle size of the Fe powder is less than or equal to 20 microns; and the pre-compacted raw material powder is placed in an FHP rapid hot pressing sintering furnace, the vacuum degree lower than 10 <-3 > Pa is kept, high-temperature rapid hot pressing sintering forming is carried out under the continuous pressure of 10-100 MPa, secondary diffusion heat treatment is carried out in the protective atmosphere after cooling, and the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material is prepared. The FH P process is adopted, the high-temperature decomposition phenomenon of the 1: 13 phase is effectively inhibited, the pure Fe powder serves as a reaction type adhesive, the magnetocaloric performance and the mechanical performance of the block are further improved, and the comprehensive performance of the material is comprehensively improved.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SOUTH CHINA TECH",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN120480174.A",
    "publicationDate": "20250815",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material based on FHP technology and preparation method of La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention relates to a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material and a preparation method thereof.The La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material is of a layered structure formed by pressing a first composition layer and a second composition layer after the first composition layer and the second composition layer are alternately stacked, the first composition layer comprises pores and a plurality of magnetocaloric phase units, the second composition layer comprises Fe or Fe alloy, and the magnetocaloric phase is La (Fe, Si) with a NaZn13 type crystal structure. Si) 13-group compounds. After the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material is subjected to high-temperature reaction, all the magnetic thermal phase units in the first composition layer are connected with one another to form an integrated structure; thus, when the La-Fe-Si-based alloy layer is inflated with hydrogen and expands, the pores play a buffering role, the situation that crystalline grains are crushed due to extrusion of crystalline grain phases is avoided, and the overall volume change of the La-Fe-Si-based alloy layer is reduced; fe or Fe alloy particles are compact, are still of a continuous layered structure and are tightly connected with the La-Fe-Si-based alloy layer, so that the obtained layered structure plays a role in inhibiting mutual separation of layers of the composite material caused by hydrogen charging, and the layered composite material after hydrogen charging basically keeps the original shape and is not broken.",
    "applicants": [
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所"
    ],
    "docId": "CN119560250.A",
    "publicationDate": "20250304",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention provides a method for preparing an anisotropic composite material through hot pressing, La-Fe-Si-based alloy powder with a certain particle size and CrMnFeCoNi alloy powder with a certain particle size are mixed in proportion and then are hot-pressed to prepare a cylindrical composite material, the main phase of the composite material is a 1: 13 pure phase of La-Fe-Si alloy, the second phase is an fcc pure phase, and the specific surface area of the composite material is 1: 10. And the second phase is in lamellar distribution and has certain directivity, so that the mechanical properties in the horizontal direction and the vertical direction are greatly different. According to the invention, reasons of Curie temperature and magnetocaloric performance changes of the composite material are researched through an X-ray diffraction pattern and element distribution; in the pressurizing process of powder metallurgy, due to the fact that the pressure transmission efficiency in the vertical direction and the pressure transmission efficiency in the horizontal direction are different, the second phase generates plastic deformation of different degrees in different directions.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV NANJING SCI & TECH",
      "南京理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN119489192.A",
    "publicationDate": "20250221",
    "title": "Method for preparing anisotropic composite material through hot pressing"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "This magnetocaloric material includes a coating powder and a resin. The coating powder is obtained by coating, with a coating film, a material powder of a La(Fe, Si)H-based compound in which hydrogen is adsorbed onto a La(Fe, Si)13-based compound. The coating film has a higher thermal conductivity and a lower hardness than the material powder. The coating films of the coating powders adjacent to each other form a mesh-like structure.",
    "applicants": [
      "MITSUBISHI ELECTRIC CORP [JP]",
      "三菱電機株式会社"
    ],
    "docId": "WO2025004169.A1",
    "publicationDate": "20250102",
    "title": "MAGNETOCALORIC MATERIAL, AND METHOD FOR PRODUCING MAGNETOCALORIC MATERIAL"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention relates to a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and a preparation method thereof.The La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material comprises a plurality of magnetocaloric phase units and a plurality of pore units, magnetocaloric phases are La (Fe, Si) 13-based phases of a NaZn13 type crystal structure, and the magnetocaloric phase units are connected to form an integrated structure. Due to the integrated structure, the defects of an interface are reduced, and magnetic heat and heat conduction loss can be reduced. And during hydrogen charging expansion, the pores play a buffering role, so that crushing caused by extrusion of crystal grains is avoided, and the purpose of no crushing during hydrogen charging is achieved.",
    "applicants": [
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所"
    ],
    "docId": "CN119207930.A",
    "publicationDate": "20241227",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and a preparation method thereof.The preparation method comprises the following steps that S1, spherical La-Fe-Si-based alloy powder and spherical Ag powder are mixed, and mixed powder is obtained; s2, sintering the mixed powder obtained in the step S1 into a block; and S3, the block obtained in the step S2 is subjected to heat treatment, and the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material is obtained. According to the method, the Ag element with the small solid solubility with the iron phase is selected and mixed with the La-Fe-Si-based alloy powder, sintering is carried out, a microstructure with La-Fe-Si particles wrapped with the Ag-rich phase is obtained, and the mechanical property of the material is improved advantageously; besides, the selected spherical La-Fe-Si-based alloy powder is beneficial for ensuring the magnetocaloric effect of the material, and meanwhile, the solid solubility of Ag in an alpha-Fe phase is relatively small, so that a large amount of Ag cannot be dissolved in a matrix in the sintering and heat treatment processes, and the excellent magnetocaloric effect can be obtained.",
    "applicants": [
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所"
    ],
    "docId": "CN119132769.A",
    "publicationDate": "20241213",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and a preparation method thereof.The preparation method comprises the steps that intermediate alloy powder rich in rare earth components is prepared at first, then the intermediate alloy powder and other raw material powder are mixed to be prepared into a target alloy, through alloy component optimization design and in combination with a specific powder metallurgy process, a magnetocaloric phase is rapidly formed within a very short sintering time, and the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material is obtained. Meanwhile, pores and a reinforcing phase exist in the material, so that the material is complete in shape and has certain strength after being charged with hydrogen.",
    "applicants": [
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所"
    ],
    "docId": "CN119008213.A",
    "publicationDate": "20241122",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a method for preparing La-Fe-Si-based alloys with different sizes through rapid solidification, the expression of the alloys is La (1-x) RxFe (11.6) Si (1.4), R is a light rare earth element and is selected from one of Ce, Nd and Pr, and # imgabs0 #. The method comprises the following steps: weighing corresponding raw materials according to the chemical formula of the alloy, and carrying out electric arc melting to obtain metal ingots; and preparing the alloy ingot into a bar or a plate by adopting a spray casting or suction casting method, sealing a pipe, carrying out heat treatment, and then carrying out water quenching. According to the method, the microscopic structure of the cross section of the alloy is represented through a scanning electron microscope, and the influence of heat conduction on the phase structure of the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy in the rapid solidification process is obtained by combining magnetic performance and magnetocaloric performance tests, so that the alloy performance change is caused.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV NANJING SCIENCE & TECH",
      "南京理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN116732427.A",
    "publicationDate": "20230912",
    "title": "Method for preparing La-Fe-Si-based alloys with different sizes through rapid solidification"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses an SPS technology-based La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material and a preparation method thereof.The preparation method comprises the following steps: uniformly mixing La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material powder and micron-sized Fe powder, and performing high-temperature spark plasma sintering molding to prepare a magnetic refrigeration block material; the sintering temperature ranges from 1100 K to 1300 K, and the pressure ranges from 10 MPa to 100 MPa; the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material is a (La1-xCex) (FeyCo1-y) 11-zSiz compound, x is larger than or equal to 0 and smaller than or equal to 0.4, y is larger than or equal to 0 and smaller than or equal to 2, z is larger than or equal to 1.0 and smaller than or equal to 1.6, the particle size of the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material is smaller than or equal to 100 microns, and the particle size of the micron-sized Fe powder is 3-5 microns. According to the method, the problem that the La-Fe-Si material is difficult to form is effectively solved. And meanwhile, the technological process is greatly simplified. The composite material prepared by the method has a good magnetocaloric effect and excellent mechanical properties at the same time.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SOUTH CHINA TECH",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN116422873.A",
    "publicationDate": "20230714",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material based on SPS technology and preparation method of La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a high-strength La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material and a preparation method thereof, a main phase of the high-strength La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material is prepared by uniformly mixing rare-earth-rich La-Fe-Si-based compound particles and an adhesive Fe powder, performing pre-forming, performing high-temperature thermal deformation forming on the pre-formed La-Fe-Si-based composite block material at 700-900 DEG C, and performing high-temperature thermal treatment in a protective atmosphere, thereby obtaining the high-strength La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material. The heat treatment temperature is 1000-1200 DEG C, and the heat treatment time is 0.5-8 hours, so that the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material is prepared. The La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material prepared by the method has a high content of 1: 13 phase and is relatively excellent in magnetocaloric performance. On the basis of powder metallurgy and heat treatment, a second rare earth-rich phase in the rare earth-rich La-Fe-Si-based alloy is adjusted into an alpha-Fe phase with good plasticity and toughness, and the mechanical property of the block composite material is remarkably improved through the evenly-distributed alpha-Fe phase.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SOUTH CHINA TECH",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN116426809.A",
    "publicationDate": "20230714",
    "title": "High-strength La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration composite material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a preparation method of a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy, which comprises the following steps: S1, designing components of the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy, and preparing raw materials according to the designed components; s2, the prepared raw materials are smelted, and a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy cast ingot is obtained; s3, the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy ingot obtained in the step S2 is subjected to plastic deformation, and a La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy blank is obtained; and S4, the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy blank obtained in the step S3 is subjected to homogenization heat treatment, and the La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy is obtained. Compared with the prior art, on the basis of a traditional cast La-Fe-Si-based alloy, the shape with the large specific surface area is obtained through plastic deformation, meanwhile, the microstructure of alpha-Fe and the microstructure of the La-rich phase are regulated and controlled, the forming rate of the magnetocaloric phase in the heat treatment process is increased, a large number of magnetocaloric phases are formed within a short time, and the large magnetocaloric effect is obtained.",
    "applicants": [
      "NINGBO INST MATERIALS TECH & ENG CAS",
      "UNIV NINGBO TECHNOLOGY",
      "中国科学院宁波材料技术与工程研究所",
      "宁波工程学院"
    ],
    "docId": "CN115109984.A",
    "publicationDate": "20220927",
    "title": "Preparation method of La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration alloy"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses an La-Fe-Si-based room temperature magnetic refrigeration composite material based on an SPS technology and a preparation method thereof. The preparation method is characterized in that La-Fe-Si-based magnetic refrigeration material powder and Pr-Co alloy powder are uniformly mixed, and formed through spark plasma sintering, the sintering temperature is 850-1100 DEG C, andthen the magnetic refrigeration composite material is obtained through tube sealing heat treatment. According to the preparation method, La-Fe-Si-based compound principal phase powder particles (magnetocaloric working medium) and Pr-Co alloy powder particles (binder) are adopted and mixed, the binder particles are heated to melt at the high sintering temperature to fill gaps between the principalphase particles, and the material porosity is reduced, so that the density of the composite material is improved, and the problem that the La-Fe-Si material is large in brittleness and is difficult toform is solved; and meanwhile, a Pr alloy element and a Co alloy element in the binder are diffused through a high-temperature diffusion process, and the obtained composite material has good magnetocaloric effect.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SOUTH CHINA TECH",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN111230112.A",
    "publicationDate": "20200605",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si-based room temperature magnetic refrigeration composite material based on SPS technology and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "[0001]    A magnetocaloric material comprising a La—Fe—Si based alloy composition that is compositionally modified to include a small but effective amount of at least one of Al, Ga, and In to improve mechanical stability of the alloy (substantially reduce alloy brittleness), improve thermal conductivity, and preserve comparable or provide improved magnetocaloric effects. The alloy composition may be further modified by inclusion of at least one of Co, Mn, Cr, and V as well as interstitial hydrogen.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV IOWA STATE RES FOUND INC [US]",
      "Iowa State University Research Foundation, Inc."
    ],
    "docId": "US2019272933.A1",
    "publicationDate": "20190905",
    "title": "Modified La—Fe—Si magnetocaloric alloys"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a lanthanum-iron-silicon-copper magnetism refrigeration material, which is excellent in magnetocaloric performance and short in preparation cycle, and a preparation method thereof. A chemical general formula of the lanthanum-iron-silicon-copper magnetism refrigeration material is (LayFe13-zSiz)100-xCux, wherein 0<x<=50, 1<=y<=2, and 0<=z<=10. The preparation method comprises the following steps that 1, La, Fe, Si and Cu are mixed according to mass percentages of the elements in the general formula; 2, under protection of high-purity argon, the prepared raw materials aresubjected to repeated smelting, cooling and overturning for four times in a vacuum arc furnace; 3, after an cast ingot is subjected to high-temperature thermal treatment at a high-purity argon atmosphere, cold water is used for quenching. A preparation technology of the material is simple, a preparation cycle of a lanthanum-iron-silicon magnetism refrigeration material is greatly shortened, according to the prepared magnetism refrigeration material, magnetic entropy increases, and magnetic hysteresis and heat hysteresis loss is little.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV BEIHANG",
      "北京航空航天大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN109266951.A",
    "publicationDate": "20190125",
    "title": "LaFeSiCu magnetism refrigeration alloy and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention provides a method for preparing La-Fe-Si fibers with high magnetic and thermal properties based on a melt thread throwing method, and belongs to the technical field of La-Fe-Si fibers. The problems of long high-temperature heat treatment time, low heat conduction efficiency and high demagnetization coefficient in use of the existing La-Fe-Si bulk alloys. The method provided by the invention comprises the following steps: 1, preparing La-Fe-Si fibers by using a La-Fe-Si alloy via the melt thread throwing method; 2, performing ultrasonic cleaning and drying on the La-Fe-Si fibers in acetone; 3, cleaning and drying a high temperature resistant ceramic tube in sequence, sealing one end of the high temperature resistant ceramic tube, performing necking processing on the high temperature resistant ceramic tube at a position 1/4 to 1/3 away from the full length of the open end, placing the fibers on the sealed side, and filling titanium wires; 4, vacuumizing, filling highly pureargon, vacuumize, repeatedly washing the gas for at least three times, and sealing the open end; and 5, performing heat treatment, cooling to the room temperature, and braking the high temperature resistant ceramic tube. By adoption of the method, a magnetocaloric material with high magnetocaloric properties, high thermal conductivity, low demagnetization coefficient and low magnetic field driveis obtained.",
    "applicants": [
      "HARBIN INST TECHNOLOGY",
      "哈尔滨工业大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN108172355.A",
    "publicationDate": "20180615",
    "title": "Method for preparing La-Fe-Si fibers with high magnetic and thermal properties based on melt thread throwing method"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention provides a La(Fe, Si)13Hx hydride magnetic refrigeration material preparation and moulding integrated method, which belongs to the technical field of a magnetic refrigeration material. The preparation and moulding integrated method is characterized in that a hydrogen storage alloy, soldering tin powder and a La(Fe, Si)13 alloy are co-processed. The processes comprise steps of fragmentation and refinement, pressurization moulding, vacuum tube sealing, and thermal treatment. The preparation and moulding integrated method is capable of successfully increasing the Curie temperature of La(Fe, Si)13, the La(Fe, Si)13 keeps giant magnetocaloric effect and has good mechanical property, compared with other hydrogen permeation methods, the preparation and moulding integrated method realizes integration of solid-state hydrogen permeation and moulding, has the advantages of simple and safe operation, environmental protection, and energy saving, and has important meaning for promotingan application of a magnetic refrigeration technology at a high-temperature region.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV XIAN TECHNOLOGY",
      "西安理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN107841293.A",
    "publicationDate": "20180327",
    "title": "La(Fe, Si)13Hx hydride magnetic refrigeration material preparation and moulding integrated method"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration composite material and a preparation method thereof. La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration material particles and tin-bismuth alloy particles are uniformly mixed and machined in a heat-mould-pressing manner to prepare the composite material. The mass ratio of La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration materials to tin-bismuth alloys is (85-90):(10-15). The La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration composite material mainly has the advantages that the composite material comprises a magnetic heat working medium and an adhesive, the porosityof the materials is reduced by the adhesive, so that the La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration composite material is high in compactness, strength and magnetocaloric effect, and the problems of high hardness, large brittleness, difficulty in machining and the like of the La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration materials are effectively solved.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV SOUTH CHINA TECH",
      "华南理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN107689278.A",
    "publicationDate": "20180213",
    "title": "La-Fe-Si based magnetic refrigeration composite material and preparation method thereof"
  },
  {
    "abstract": "The invention discloses a preparation method of La (Fe, Si) 13Hx hydride magnetic refrigeration materials. The preparation method includes the steps: selecting a solid hydride, and respectively performing ball milling, crushing and refining for the solid hydride and La (Fe, Si) 13Hx alloys; uniformly mixing two kinds of refined powder, and performing pressing and forming for the mixed powder to obtain block-shaped materials; performing vacuum sealing tube for the formed block-shaped materials, performing heat treatment for the block-shaped materials in a heating furnace to obtain the La (Fe, Si) 13Hx hydride magnetic refrigeration materials. The decomposition temperature of the solid hydride is lower than that of the La (Fe, Si) 13Hx alloys, and the heat treatment temperature is in between the decomposition temperature of the solid hydride and the decomposition temperature of the La (Fe, Si) 13Hx alloys. According to the method, solid seepage hydrogen is achieved, the Curie temperature of La (Fe, Si) 13 can be successfully improved, giant magnetocaloric effects can be kept, and solid seepage hydrogen is simple to operate and low in potential safety hazard as compared with gas seepage hydrogen.",
    "applicants": [
      "UNIV XIAN TECHNOLOGY",
      "西安理工大学"
    ],
    "docId": "CN106782968.A",
    "publicationDate": "20170531",
    "title": "Preparation method of La (Fe, Si) 13Hx hydride magnetic refrigeration materials"
  }
]

